 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 459849,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<table class=\"unnumbered full-width\">\n<thead>\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\"><strong>Dataset E Description</strong></td>\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\"><strong>Data</strong></td>\n\n</tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"left\">Salaries for employees at a technology company (in dollars)</td>\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"left\">Sample of 10 employees: $72,500; $84,300; $58,900; $55,100; $82,000; $94,600; $82,200; $104,600; $63,800; $77,500</td>\n\n</tr></tbody>\n\n</table>\nFor Dataset E, determine the percentile for the employee with a salary of $82,000. Round your answer to the nearest whole number percentile.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "To calculate percentiles for a specific data value in a dataset, first order the dataset from smallest to largest and count the number of data values in the dataset. Locate the measurement of interest and count how many data values fall below the measurement.<br>\nFor the given dataset, there are 10 data values, and $82,000 represents the sixth data value in the ordered listing. Thus, there are 5 data values below $82,000. Then the percentile for the measurement is calculated as follows:<br>\n<span data-math=\"\\text{percentile}=\\;\\frac{\\text{number of data values below the measurement}}{\\text{total number of data values}}\\cdot100\\%=\\frac5{10}\\cdot100\\%=50\\%\"></span> "
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\text{Percentile}\\;=\\;50\\%\"></span> "
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
